    rdf:value """Thursday May 6. 1897. Villa Rosa. Fiesole
All day in train. 
x x x x x x x
no entries after May 6 until May 27:
Thursday May 27.97, Villa Rosa. 
I will not say anything about this interval, which has been full of sorrow. We are now busy house-hunting, as we are driven out by Kraus’ Brass Band, and today we looked at villas at La Pietra, Montughi, and Castello. But I think we shall stick to our own Fiesole hill. Mr. Morgan came to call, and remained to dinner. We read Pater’s “Demeter and Persephone” after he had gone. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 125 ;
